From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 05:41:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: report the GPU
 temperature placeholders as no data

The J604 SMC exposes 18 GPU temperature keys (Tg0C/D, G/H, K/L, O/P,
U/V, X/Y, d/e, j/k, m/n). Each pair reads -4.5 C and 0.8 C, always:
the same values are in the macOS 27.0.1 key dump, and on Linux they do
not move with the GPU idle or under load. The GPU heat shows up in TVMS
and the Ts0x keys instead. Temperature discovery listed the placeholders
as temperatures, so sensors showed a GPU at -4.5 C.

Describe the keys with apple,no-data-below-millicelsius, as the M4 Pro
MacBook Pros do for their GPU keys, so macsmc-hwmon reports no data for
them instead of a false reading.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 115 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 115 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index af48874a3a..b9db4934d2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -977,6 +977,121 @@
 		apple,key-id = "TCMz";
 		label = "CPU Die Hottest";
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The SMC GPU temperature keys hold placeholders on the J604: -4.5 C on
+	 * the first key of each pair and 0.8 C on the second, the same values in
+	 * the macOS 27.0.1 key dump and on Linux with the GPU idle or under
+	 * load. The GPU heat shows up in TVMS and Ts0x instead. Report these as
+	 * no data rather than as GPU temperatures, as for the M4 Pro.
+	 */
+	temperature-Tg0C {
+		apple,key-id = "Tg0C";
+		label = "GPU Tg0C";
+		apple,no-data-below-millicelsius = <10000>;
+	};
+
